{"id":"project-LICHEN-worker6-9n2n","title":"[review] project-LICHEN-worker6-bkfv: mark_response_used before encryption completion can permanently consume request PIV on failure","description":"## Location
`rust/lichen-oscore/src/lib.rs:981` — `Context::protect_response()`, the no-PIV response branch.

## Problem
`self.mark_response_used(request_seq)` is called at line 981 **before** encryption completes. If any subsequent step fails (heapless `extend_from_slice` overflow at line ~1000, AES-CCM encryption failure), the replay window is permanently advanced but no response ciphertext is produced.

```rust
} else {
    let request_seq =
        OscoreSeqNum::from_piv(request_piv).ok_or(OscoreError::InvalidParam)?;
    self.mark_response_used(request_seq);  // <-- TOO EARLY, no rollback

    let mut piv = [0u8; PIV_MAX_LEN];
    piv[..request_piv.len()].copy_from_slice(request_piv);
    (piv, request_piv.len(), None)
};
// ... encryption follows, can fail after the mark ...
```

## Impact
- The caller cannot retry the same request PIV after a transient encryption failure
- A future valid attempt with the same PIV is wrongly rejected as `OscoreError::Replay`
- DOS vector: repeated failures permanently burn request PIVs

## Fix
Move `mark_response_used` to AFTER successful encryption, or implement a rollback on the error path. Since `compute_nonce` is infallible and the only remaining failure points are buffer sizing and AES-CCM (both predictable), a deferred-mark approach is cleanest: mark immediately before returning the `Ok` tuple.","status":"open","priority":0,"issue_type":"bug","owner":"agent@lichen-project.dev","created_at":"2026-07-24T17:21:16.407364788Z","created_by":"AI Agent","updated_at":"2026-07-24T17:21:16.407364788Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"project-LICHEN-worker6-9n2n","depends_on_id":"project-LICHEN-worker6-bkfv","type":"discovered-from","created_at":"2026-07-24T17:21:16.550455833Z","created_by":"AI Agent","metadata":"{}"}]}

